<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Bids remain mixed.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Bids remain mixed.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dark northern spring wheat cash bids remained mixed on Thursday in quiet activity.</p>
<p>&quot;The basis felt a little bit softer and receipts were not anything huge but there were a few more trains down on the floor for sale than what we expected,&quot; one Minneapolis dealer said.</p>
<p>He noted that short term needs for spring wheat have been fulfilled. Now users are waiting to see what the farmers going to do. &quot;Farmers have been sitting tight,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>MGE December wheat firmed 1/4 cent at $4.13-3/4 a bushel.</p>
<p>In the Pacific Northwest movement, which had been active in the last day or so, has been quiet, another dealer said.  </p>
